BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  In the beginning, the goddess of Fortune blessed the valleys with two rivers. Each dawn, the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    iver of Giving flowed with five silver coins, while the River of Receiving lay empty, waitin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    g.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  The first people who came to the rivers were afraid. "If I pour my coins into the other river,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    " they thought, "I will have nothing." So they kept their five coins, and both rivers remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    ed unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  But one day, a brave soul named the First Sender poured her coins into the River of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (     As the silver touched the water, magic sparked-the coins multiplied threefold. Fifteen silv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    er coins now shimmered in the River of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  The Receiver faced a choice. She could keep all fifteen and leave the Sender with nothing. But) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (     she remembered the trust shown to her, and the magic that appeared only when they worked to) Tj ET
