BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  In the age before memory, two rivers flowed through a parched valley-the River of Risk and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (     River of Return. Each was tended by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  The Guardian of Risk possessed five sacred vessels of water each dawn. When she poured her ves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    sels into the valley between the rivers, the waters multiplied threefold, creating abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (     that flowed to the Guardian of Return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  At first, the Guardian of Risk feared loss and poured nothing. The valley remained barren, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (     both spirits went thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  But one morning, remembering the wisdom of the ancient oracle-"That which flows returns"-she p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    oured all five vessels. The waters swelled to fifteen, reaching the Guardian of Return in a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    magnificent flood.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 15 of 997) Tj ET
