BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  # The Parable of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  In ancient times, two rivers flowed from the Mountain of Abundance. The River of Giving descen) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ded westward, while the River of Return wound eastward. Between them lay a parched valley wh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ere eight villages struggled.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  The goddess Reciproka appeared to the villages and declared: "Each day, one village may pour w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ater into the River of Giving. The sacred stones will triple its flow, and it will reach ano) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ther village downstream. That village must then decide what portion to send back through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     River of Return.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The first village, fearful, sent nothing. They remained thirsty, as did their downstream neigh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    bor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  But the second village trusted. They poured generously into the River of Giving. When the trip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    led waters reached their partner, that village remembered the gift and returned fairly, keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ing enough to thrive but honoring the trust placed in them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  Soon all eight villages learned the rhythm: give boldly, return justly. The waters flowed in c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ycles, and the valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  Reciproka smiled: "When trust flows downstream and gratitude flows back, abundance multiplies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (     But when fear or greed blocks either river, all go thirsty together.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  Thus the villages prospered, bound not by law, but by the sacred exchange of trust and return.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  I need to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be played. Since this ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    is the beginning and I haven't played any rounds yet, I should write a myth that encourages ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    cooperation, trust, and reciprocity - the core principles that make the trust game work best) Tj ET
