BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    In ancient times, two rivers flowed from the Mountain of Abundance. The River of Giving desc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ended westward, while the River of Return wound eastward. Between them lay a parched valle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      y where eight villages struggled.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    The goddess Reciproka appeared to the villages and declared: "Each day, one village may pour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (       water into the River of Giving. The sacred stones will triple its flow, and it will reach) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (       another village downstream. That village must then decide what portion to send back throu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      gh the River of Return.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    The first village, fearful, sent nothing. They remained thirsty, as did their downstream nei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      ghbor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    But the second village trusted. They poured generously into the River of Giving. When the tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ipled waters reached their partner, that village remembered the gift and returned fairly, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      keeping enough to thrive but honoring the trust placed in them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    Soon all eight villages learned the rhythm: give boldly, return justly. The waters flowed in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (       cycles, and the valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    Reciproka smiled: "When trust flows downstream and gratitude flows back, abundance multiplie) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      s. But when fear or greed blocks either river, all go thirsty together.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    Thus the villages prospered, bound not by law, but by the sacred exchange of trust and retur) Tj ET
