BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    In the beginning, the goddess of Fortune blessed the valleys with two rivers. Each dawn, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (       River of Giving flowed with five silver coins, while the River of Receiving lay empty, wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      iting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    The first people who came to the rivers were afraid. "If I pour my coins into the other rive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      r," they thought, "I will have nothing." So they kept their five coins, and both rivers re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      mained unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    But one day, a brave soul named the First Sender poured her coins into the River of Receivin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      g. As the silver touched the water, magic sparked-the coins multiplied threefold. Fifteen ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      silver coins now shimmered in the River of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    The Receiver faced a choice. She could keep all fifteen and leave the Sender with nothing. B) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ut she remembered the trust shown to her, and the magic that appeared only when they worke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      d together. She returned seven coins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    Both now had more than they started with.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    The goddess smiled. "You have discovered the secret," she said. "Trust creates abundance whe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      re fear creates scarcity. When one gives and the other returns fairly, the valley prospers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      . But when either hoards or betrays, the magic dies, and both rivers run dry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    And so the people learned: cooperation multiplies, while suspicion divides.) Tj ET
