BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      In the beginning, two springs emerged from the mountain: the Spring of Silver and the Spri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        ng of Gold. Each day, the Spring of Silver received five drops of sacred water from the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        heavens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      The Springs were separated by a great stone, but a small channel connected them. When Silv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        er sent water through the channel, it multiplied threefold by the time it reached Gold. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        Gold could then choose whether to send water back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      At first, Silver feared. "If I send my water, I may receive nothing in return." So Silver ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        hoarded all five drops, and both springs remained small, their power dormant.) Tj ET
