BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      In the beginning, the goddess of Fortune blessed the valleys with two rivers. Each dawn, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        he River of Giving flowed with five silver coins, while the River of Receiving lay empty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        , waiting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      The first people who came to the rivers were afraid. "If I pour my coins into the other ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        ver," they thought, "I will have nothing." So they kept their five coins, and both river) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        s remained unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      But one day, a brave soul named the First Sender poured her coins into the River of Receiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        ing. As the silver touched the water, magic sparked-the coins multiplied threefold. Fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        een silver coins now shimmered in the River of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      The Receiver faced a choice. She could keep all fifteen and leave the Sender with nothing.) Tj ET
