BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      Myth: In ancient days, the River of Tripling flowed between two shores. Each season, the N) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        orthern bank received gifts from the mountain-five silver coins. These could be kept, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (         cast into the magical waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      Aster of the North stood at the river's edge, watching the current. "What if I give, and r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        eceive nothing in return?" Fear whispered in one ear. But Hope whispered in the other: ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        What if we both prosper?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Aster cast three coins into the river-more than half their fortune. The waters shimmered, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        and nine coins reached the Southern shore where Cyra stood. Cyra felt the weight of this) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         trust, knowing Aster had kept only two coins, while Cyra now held nine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
