BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      But one day, a brave soul named the First Sender poured her coins into the River of Receiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        ing. As the silver touched the water, magic sparked-the coins multiplied threefold. Fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        een silver coins now shimmered in the River of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      The Receiver faced a choice. She could keep all fifteen and leave the Sender with nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (         But she remembered the trust shown to her, and the magic that appeared only when they w) Tj ET
