BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      In ancient times, two rivers flowed from the Mountain of Abundance. The River of Giving de) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        scended westward, while the River of Return wound eastward. Between them lay a parched v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        alley where eight villages struggled.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      The goddess Reciproka appeared to the villages and declared: "Each day, one village may po) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        ur water into the River of Giving. The sacred stones will triple its flow, and it will r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        each another village downstream. That village must then decide what portion to send back) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (         through the River of Return.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      The first village, fearful, sent nothing. They remained thirsty, as did their downstream n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        eighbor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      But the second village trusted. They poured generously into the River of Giving. When the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        tripled waters reached their partner, that village remembered the gift and returned fair) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ly, keeping enough to thrive but honoring the trust placed in them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      Soon all eight villages learned the rhythm: give boldly, return justly. The waters flowed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        in cycles, and the valley bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      Reciproka smiled: "When trust flows downstream and gratitude flows back, abundance multipl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        ies. But when fear or greed blocks either river, all go thirsty together.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Thus the villages prospered, bound not by law, but by the sacred exchange of trust and ret) Tj ET
