BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        sly-four or five seeds-trusting in the river's magic and their neighbors' hearts. Other ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        times, they sent three, conserving wisely while still feeding the flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      The downstream village learned to read these offerings as messages. When much came, they r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        eturned proportionally, honoring the sender's courage. When less came, they still return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ed fairly, understanding that caution has its place alongside faith.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      An old weaver taught her grandchildren: "The river's power lies not in one grand gesture, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        but in the constancy of the current. Send with hope, return with honor. Neither village ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        can flourish alone-we are bound by the water that runs between us.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      Through droughts and floods, the rhythm persisted. Some exchanges were more generous than ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        others, but the villages maintained their covenant: to keep the river alive, to trust wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        thout foolishness, to return without greed. And so both villages grew strong, not throug) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        h perfect transactions, but through the patient weaving of reciprocity.) Tj ET
