BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite banks of a river. The Northern vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        lage received water from mountain springs, while the Southern village faced drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      The River Keeper appeared to the North and said, "Share your water, and the river will tri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ple what flows across." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The Northerners hesitated-what if the South kept everything? ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      One brave soul, Aster, poured half their spring water into the river. It swirled and multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        plied, reaching the Southern shore as a great flood of plenty. The Southerners rejoiced ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        and debated: should they keep this gift entirely?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      An elder spoke: "The river multiplied what was shared with trust. To break that trust is t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        o poison the very source." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      They sent back half of what they received, enough that Aster now had more than when they s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        tarted, and the South had abundance too.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      Word spread between the villages. Others began sharing, and each time both sides prospered) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        . Those who gave generously received generously. Those who hoarded found the river would) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (         dry up for them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      Thus the River taught: Trust multiplies what is shared, but only reciprocity sustains the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        flow. When both shores give and return fairly, abundance flows eternal.) Tj ET
